Quiz02_00: 20 points

############################################################

Quiz02_01: 50 points
(FnA1szLongestMonoSubsequence)
Please state the status of this question:
2. Solved with testing.
Use dynamic programming from right to left. For each index i,
scan every j > i once and compute the length of the best
nondecreasing subsequence starting at i; break ties toward the
smaller next index so the final answer is leftmost. This is O(n^2).
  
############################################################

Quiz02_02: 50 points
(sort1000WithNoRecursion)
Please state the status of this question:
2. Solved with testing.
Use iterative insertion-sort on the array. No recursion is used.

############################################################

Quiz02_03: 50 points
(Soduku_dfs_solve and Soduku_bfs_solve)
Please state the status of this question:
2. Solved with testing.
Represent a Game-of-24 state as a list of remaining terms. Each child
combines one pair of terms with +, -, *, or / and reduces the list size
by one. DFS/BFS directly call DFirstEnumerate/BFirstEnumerate on this tree
and filter the leaves whose single remaining term evaluates to 24.

############################################################

Please choose only ONE from Quiz02_04 and Quiz02_05.
If unspecified, I assume by default that Quiz02_04 is
chosen.

############################################################

Quiz02_04:
30 points plus up to 20 bonus points
(isAVL and genAVLBST)
Please state the status of this question:
2. Solved with testing.
For isAVL, do one postorder traversal and return either the subtree
height or failure. For the maximal-height question, use the standard
minimal-node AVL recurrence S(h)=1+S(h-1)+S(h-2) and find the largest
h with S(h) <= 1,000,000, which gives height 28.

############################################################

Quiz02_05:
30 points plus up to 20 bonus points
(isRBT and genRedBlackBST)
Please state the status of this question:
2. Solved with testing.
For isRBT, do one traversal that checks the red-parent rule and equal
black heights on both subtrees. For the black-height question, use the
fact that a red-black tree of black-height b has at most 2^(2b)-1
internal nodes, so 1,000,000 keys require black-height 10.

############################################################

Quiz02_06: 50 points
(reroot and insert on DBST)
Please state the status of this question:
2. Solved with testing.
Insert is standard BST leaf insertion with parent pointers and subtree
size updates. reroot selects a random node by rank using stored sizes,
then rotates it upward until it becomes the root.

